  "decision_conditions": [
    "Occupier",
    "The development must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date hereof.\r\rReason: To comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, as amended.",
    "All external facing materials, treatments and finishes shall be similar to those of the original building and maintained and retained thereafter. This applies unless differences are shown on the drawings we have approved. \r\rReason: To ensure that the extension harmonises with the existing building and to ensure compliance with Policy 28 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018.",
    "The development must be carried out in accordance with the provisions of the Planning Fire Safety Strategy.\r\rReason: To ensure that the development incorporates the necessary fire safety measures in accordance with the Mayor's London Plan Policy D12.",
    "No development, excluding site clearance and demolition works, shall take place until a detailed flood risk assessment (FRA) must be submitted to the Local Planning Authority and approved in writing. The submitted FRA must:\r(i) provide estimated flood levels and depths in the 1 in 100-year event (+ 17% for climate change) in accordance with Government Standing Advice for Minor Extensions;\r(ii) confirm that floor levels for the proposed extension are set and that flood resistant materials will be used at least 600 millimetres (mm) above the estimated flood level;\r(iii) provide updated details of all proposed flood resilience measures to be incorporated as part of the design and layout of the extension;\r(iv) Have regard to the relevant British Standards and guidance in the Construction Industry Research and Information Association (CIRIA) 'Property Flood Resilience Code of Practice'.\r\rReason: To comply with Government Standing Advice and Policy 31 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018.",
    "The development hereby approved shall be constructed in accordance with the approved Flood Risk Assessment as amended. Prior to occupation, written confirmation that the approved flood resilience measures, have been implemented as part of the extension as built must be submitted to the Local Planning Authority and approved in writing. All of the approved measures must thereafter be retained for as long as the development is in existence. \r\rReason: To comply with Government Standing Advice and Policy 31 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018."
  ],
